(An hour later, back in the treehouse, the Keystone hangs suspended over a rumbling) Tj
T*
(hearth-fire. The Custodian, older now, exhaustion plain in her voice, folds herself into) Tj
T*
(an over-stuffed chair. "You fought hard. I'm not surprised. Emeris doesn't send just) Tj
T*
(anyone." She lets you sit with it, the warmth and the weight both. And then, because) Tj
T*
(there is always one more thing: she has a question about what you will tell the people) Tj
T*
(who sent you, and a map to somewhere the light is going wrong.) Tj
